STABLE
------

0.5.0
-----
Distribution 0.5.0 ships `test_factory` 0.5.0 and `test_factory_pgtap` 0.1.0.

NOTE: There is no `ALTER EXTENSION` update path to 0.5.0. That covers both
`test_factory` 0.3.1 (from distribution 0.4.2) and unreleased 0.5.0 installs
taken from git; drop and recreate the extension instead.

== Install without a superuser (`superuser = false`)
Both extensions can now be installed by a role with `CREATEROLE` and
`CREATE` on the target database, e.g. RDS/Aurora's master user, instead of
requiring a real superuser.

== Fix `CREATE EXTENSION test_factory` on PG16+ for non-superusers
On PG16+ a non-superuser install failed with `must be able to SET ROLE
"test_factory__owner"`: `CREATE ROLE` doesn't give its creator SET-enabled
membership in the new role. Install now grants it when missing, and raises
a clear error with a suggested `GRANT` when the installer can't grant it
itself. Fixes #14.

== Fix install failures caused by the `original_role` temp table
Both install scripts saved the caller's role in an `ON COMMIT DROP` temp
table, which became extension-owned and broke `CREATE EXTENSION
test_factory_pgtap` on PG17 (#12) and inside an explicit transaction (#13).
They now use a transaction-local setting instead. `test_factory_pgtap`'s
0.1.0 install script was fixed in place: the objects it creates are
unchanged, so its version stays 0.1.0.

== Point META resources at the current repository
Homepage, bug tracker and repository links now point at
https://github.com/Postgres-Extensions/test_factory.
